duced diversity\n   - In dialogue: interruption that resets attention\""}], :conclusion "Shock awakens and resets; it breaks inertia and renews motion.", :directives {:audience "improvisers, system designers, CT practitioners", :sigils ["💤/也"], :style "pattern", :title "䷲ 震 (Zhèn) - The Arousing (Thunder)", :tone "foundational"}, :id "iching/hexagram-51-zhen", :keywords [], :projection-version "flexiarg-v0", :references [], :scores {}, :sigils ["💤/也"], :source-path "library/iching/hexagram-51-zhen.flexiarg", :sources [], :status :ok, :title "䷲ 震 (Zhèn) - The Arousing (Thunder)", :typed-slots nil} #:pattern{:clauses [{:name "conclusion", :name-key "conclusion", :slug "conclusion", :text "Stillness halts motion to restore clarity; it prevents rash action."} {:name "context", :name-key "context", :slug "context", :text "A system needs to pause to regain stability or avoid error."} {:name "IF", :name-key "if", :slug "if", :text "    Motion is causing confusion or harm."} {:name "HOWEVER", :name-key "however", :slug "however", :text "    Too much stillness becomes paralysis."} {:name "THEN", :name-key "then", :slug "then", :text "    Halt briefly, observe, then resume with renewed alignment."} {:name "BECAUSE", :name-key "because", :slug "because", :text "    Stillness is the boundary that preserves order when action destabilizes."} {:name "evidence", :name-key "evidence", :slug "evidence", :text "Traditional: \"Keeping still. It is favorable to remain steadfast.\""} {:name "NEXT-STEPS", :name-key "next-steps", :slug "next-steps", :text "    - Identify the boundary where action should stop.\n    - Pause long enough to reset.\n    - Pair with ䷲ (震) to restart motion.\n\n@ct-interpretation\n  :vision\n  {:objects #{:moving :still}\n   :morphism {:id :halt\n              :source :moving\n              :target :still\n              :type :boundary}}\n\n  :as-morphism\n  {:domain :active-state\n   :codomain :paused-state\n   :preservation :high\n   :composition :resets-motion