*.flexiarg`: lint for required metadata, forbid renaming the clause markers, and add CI that refuses commits lacking `@sigils`, `@references`, or the standard clause order; every pattern added to `resources/pattern_store.edn` must cite the lint status", :directives {:keywords ["template" "lint" "metadata" "structure" "format" "CI" "validate" "standard" "machine-readable"], :references ["devmap-coherence/prototype-alignment-embedding" "stack-coherence/readme-devmap-sync"], :sigils ["🐺/万" "🔃/习"], :title "Canon Template Discipline"}, :id "library-coherence/library-template-discipline", :keywords ["template" "lint" "metadata" "structure" "format" "CI" "validate" "standard" "machine-readable"], :projection-version "flexiarg-v0", :references ["devmap-coherence/prototype-alignment-embedding" "stack-coherence/readme-devmap-sync"], :scores {}, :sigils ["🐺/万" "🔃/习"], :source-path "library/library-coherence/library-template-discipline.flexiarg", :sources [], :status :ok, :title "Canon Template Discipline", :typed-slots nil} #:pattern{:clauses [{:name "conclusion", :name-key "conclusion", :slug "conclusion", :text "Use an LLM to assemble a coherent argument from pattern summaries when library ordering is unclear."} {:name "context", :name-key "context", :slug "context", :text "You are reviewing a library where patterns should scaffold a coherent argument but the ordering is implicit or missing."} {:name "IF", :name-key "if", :slug "if", :text "    The library’s argument exists in fragments across pattern summaries (!conclusion or devmap instantiated-by lines)."} {:name "HOWEVER", :name-key "however", :slug "however", :text "    Readers may not infer the argument without an explicit narrative flow."} {:name "THEN", :name-key "then", :slug "then", :text "    Use an LLM to scan the summary fields, cluster related claims, order them into a draft argument, and read it back for coherence and gaps."} {:name "BECAUSE", :name-key "because", :slug "because", :text "    LLMs are strong at