nce that listeners and bridges are functioning continuously, not just at join time."} {:name "HOWEVER", :name-key "however", :slug "however", :text "    A simple ping is ambiguous (didn't hear, busy, crashed, wrong channel), and manual checking does not scale."} {:name "THEN", :name-key "then", :slug "then", :text "    Require heartbeats: each agent emits a heartbeat every T seconds containing session-id, transport, last-received-seq, last-sent-seq, and current-mode; the moderator HUD flags stalls after N misses or when stale for S seconds and emits a stall event with the reason; stalled instances must reconnect or shut down."} {:name "BECAUSE", :name-key "because", :slug "because", :text "    Liveness without sequence context does not distinguish quiet from partitioned."} {:name "NEXT-STEPS", :name-key "next-steps", :slug "next-steps", :text "    - evidence: tune heartbeat period vs noise and false alarms.\n    - evidence: record false positives/negatives.\n    - evidence: correlate stalls with actual bridge failures.\n    - evidence: measure time-to-stall detection vs real outage.\n    - evidence-shape: {:session/id :string, :transport :keyword, :last-received-seq :int, :last-sent-seq :int, :mode :keyword, :heartbeat/seconds :int, :missed/count :int, :missed/threshold :int, :stale/seconds :int, :grace/seconds :int, :stall/flagged? :boolean, :stall/reason :keyword, :stall/ts :string, :ts :string}"}], :conclusion "Make liveness a first-class signal via periodic heartbeats tied to sequence numbers.", :directives {:audience "fulab agents, musn server", :sigils ["💗/七"], :style "pattern", :title "Require Liveness Heartbeats With Sequence Context", :tone "technical"}, :id "realtime/liveness-heartbeats", :keywords [], :projection-version "flexiarg-v0", :references [], :scores {}, :sigils ["💗/七"], :source-path "library/realtime/liveness-heartbeats.flexiarg", :sources [], :status :ok, :title "Require Liveness Heartbeats With Sequence Context", :typed-slots nil} #:pattern{:c