h explicit transitions (DISCUSS→DIAGNOSE→EXECUTE) and exit criteria; only EXECUTE permits repo changes and it requires a human-issued token or explicit approval; EXECUTE must end with an explicit exit back to DISCUSS plus a brief summary; define a reset/timeout (e.g., human RESET or TTL) to prevent stuck modes."} {:name "BECAUSE", :name-key "because", :slug "because", :text "    Mixing coordination talk with action talk collapses accountability and makes it hard to reconstruct why changes happened."} {:name "NEXT-STEPS", :name-key "next-steps", :slug "next-steps", :text "    - evidence: tag every message with mode.\n    - evidence: review sessions where mode drift occurred.\n    - evidence: validate whether gating reduces surprise changes and improves auditability.\n    - evidence: track time spent in each mode and reasons for transitions.\n    - evidence-shape: {:mode :keyword, :mode/from :keyword, :mode/to :keyword, :mode/exit :keyword, :mode/exit-criteria :string, :mode/ttl-seconds :int, :approval/token :string, :actor :string, :ts :string}"}], :conclusion "Separate chat from work by requiring an explicit mode switch before code-changing actions.", :directives {:audience "fulab agents, musn server", :sigils ["💖/下"], :style "pattern", :title "Gate Code Changes Behind Explicit Modes", :tone "technical"}, :id "realtime/mode-gate", :keywords [], :projection-version "flexiarg-v0", :references [], :scores {}, :sigils ["💖/下"], :source-path "library/realtime/mode-gate.flexiarg", :sources [], :status :ok, :title "Gate Code Changes Behind Explicit Modes", :typed-slots nil} #:pattern{:clauses [{:name "conclusion", :name-key "conclusion", :slug "conclusion", :text "Start work only after a signed hello+ack handshake confirms coherent reception."} {:name "context", :name-key "context", :slug "context", :text "Realtime multi-agent coding sessions (human + 2+ agents) over IRC/WS bridges can silently fail."} {:name "IF", :name-key "if", :slug "if", :text "    You need to know who