research — and\n                 by mapping the stakeholders and values that shape it."} {:name "because", :name-key "because", :slug "because", :text "A research repository is not merely a storage system but the\n             institutional surface where research practices are made public,\n             accountable, and citable."} {:name "because", :name-key "because", :slug "because", :text "The research lifecycle at OBU spans multiple external systems."} {:name "because", :name-key "because", :slug "because", :text "The research ecosystem is shaped by the people who interact with it."} {:name "because", :name-key "because", :slug "because", :text "Institutional values establish what \"good\" research infrastructure\n             is assumed to mean."} {:name "because", :name-key "because", :slug "because", :text "Identity and expectations remain tacit unless explicitly mapped."}], :conclusion "Our stated values and stakeholder roles form the identity space [🌹/门 🌆/文]\n              from which all repository behaviours emerge — and the repository\n              itself is the institutional surface where this identity becomes visible.", :directives {:sigils ["🌹/门" "🌆/文"], :title "Repository Identity Space"}, :id "repository-transition/identity-space", :keywords [], :projection-version "flexiarg-v0", :references [], :scores {}, :sigils ["🌹/门" "🌆/文"], :source-path "library/repository-transition/identity-space.flexiarg", :sources [], :status :ok, :title "Repository Identity Space", :typed-slots nil} #:pattern{:clauses [{:name "conclusion", :name-key "conclusion", :slug "conclusion", :text "Role × Value invariants that must be preserved in transformation"} {:name "THEN", :name-key "then", :slug "then", :text "Operate an explicit move on the named axis (see substructure below); steward the pattern against the declared discipline."} {:name "lemma", :name-key "lemma", :slug "lemma", :text "Infrastructure must support plural forms of visibility and contribution."} {:name "lemma", :name-key "lemma", :slug "lemma", :text "The repository must make research trustworthy by design."} {:name "lemma", :name-key "lemma", :slug "lemma", :text "Infrastructure must support flexible, linkable, cross-disciplinary reuse."} {:name "lemma", :name-key "lemma", :slug "lemma", :text "The repository must reduce friction and support sharing without penalty."} {:name "because", :name-key "because", :slug "because", :text "We ARE diverse stakeholders interacting with the research ecosystem,\n             and we BELIEVE in Inclusivity,"} {:name "because", :name-key "because", :slug "because", :text "We ARE accountable actors (Governance, Assessors, Archivists, Students),\n             and we BELIEVE in Confidence and Responsibility,"} {:name "because", :name-key "because", :slug "because", :text "We ARE creators (Depositors) and reusers (Downloaders),\n             and we BELIEVE in Enterprising Creativity and Connectedness,"} {:name "because", :name-key "because", :slug "because", :text "We ARE a community producing and sharing research,\n             and we BELIEVE in Generosity of Spirit,"}], :conclusion "Role × Value invariants that must be preserved in transformation", :directives {:sigils ["👓/支" "🌱/门"], :title "Role × Value Invariants"}, :id "repository-transition/invariants", :keywords [], :projection-version "flexiarg-v0", :references [], :scores {}, :sigils ["👓/支" "🌱/门"], :source-path "library/repository-transition/invariants.flexiarg", :sources [], :status :ok, :title "Role × Value Invariants", :typed-slots nil} #:pattern{:clauses [{:name "conclusion", :name-key "conclusion", :slug "conclusion", :text "A repository transition is best led using a lightweight, iterative [👉/义 🌹/门]\n              identity→projection→capability process."} {:name "THEN", :name-key "then", :slug "then", :text "Operate an explicit move on the named axis (see substructure below); steward the pattern against the declared discipline."} {:name "underpinned-by", :name-key "underpinned-by", :slug "underpinned-by", :text "This model aligns with OBU identity AND with PCE capability\n                      expectations."} {:name "because", :name-key "because", :slug "because", :text "Repository behaviour emerges from stakeholders acting through the\n             university’s guiding principles."} {:name "because", :name-key "because", :slug "because", :text "Identity alone does not determine behaviour; it is always projected\n             into PCE-defined capability dimensions."} {:name "because", :name-key "because", :slug "because", :text "These tensions can be used as design signals with a simple,\n             repeatable leadership pattern."}], :conclusion "A repository transition is best led using a lightweight, iterative [👉/义 🌹/门]\n              identity→projection→capability process.", :directives {:sigils ["👉/义" "🌹/门"], :title "Repository Transition Job Argument"}, :id "repository-transition/job-argument", :keywords [], :projection-version "flexiarg-v0", :references [], :scores {}, :sigils ["👉/义" "🌹/门"], :source-path "library/repository-transition/job-argument.flexiarg", :sources [], :status :ok, :title "Repository Transition Job Argument", :typed-slots nil} #:pattern{:clauses [{:name "conclusion", :name-key "conclusion", :slug "conclusion", :text "The current distortions in identity-space project into PCE-space as [🔥/亏 🌹/门]\n              systemic misalignments that threaten research culture if unaddressed."} {:name "THEN", :name-key "then", :slug "then", :text "Operate an explicit move on the named axis (see substructure below); steward the pattern against the declared discipline.\n\nCareer development and professional growth are hindered by the\n                   repository’s operational design.\n\nIf left unchecked, the current projection of identity distortions into\n                 PCE space results in a viable-system failure: reduced sustainability,\n                 weakened integrity, fragmented connectivity, compromised inclusivity,\n                 and stunted development."} {:name "because", :name-key "because", :slug "because", :text "Strategy becomes reactive rather than robust."} {:name "because", :name-key "because", :slug "because", :text "Responsibility is inconsistently expressed across the system."} {:name "because", :name-key "because", :slug "because", :text "Connectivity becomes siloed and brittle."} {:name "because", :name-key "because", :slug "because", :text "Inclusivity is reduced to aspiration rather than practice."} {:name "because", :name-key "because", :slug "because", :text "Development pathways are constrained by system friction."}], :conclusion "The current distortions in identity-space project into PCE-space as [🔥/亏 🌹/门]\n              systemic misalignments that threaten research culture if unaddressed.", :directives {:sigils ["🔥/亏" "🌹/门"], :title "Strawman Misalignment Map"}, :id "repository-transition/strawman", :keywords [], :projection-version "flexiarg-v0", :references [], :scores {}, :sigils ["🔥/亏" "🌹/门"], :source-path "library/repository-transition/strawman.flexiarg", :sources [], :status :ok, :title "Strawman Misalignment Map", :typed-slots nil} #:pattern{:clauses [{:name "conclusion", :name-key "conclusion", :slug "conclusion", :text "Leadership Patterns Underpinning the Transformation Cycle"} {:name "THEN", :name-key "then", :slug "then", :text "Operate an explicit move on the named axis (see substructure below); steward the pattern against the declared discipline.\n\nLeadership must match connection mode to context and collaborator.\n\nThe transformation cycle is not just procedural (tensions → requirements → transparency → feedback → iteration).\n                 It is relational, adjusting compatibility, rhythm, worldshape, boundaries,\n                 and connection modes to guide the institution through change."} {:name "clarifies", :name-key "clarifies", :slug "clarifies", :text "Emotional economies and meaning structures matter for change readiness."} {:name "lemma", :name-key "lemma", :slug "lemma", :text "Closed-loop teams improve through real-time collaboration (e.g., librarians + RDM)."} {:name "lemma", :name-key "lemma", :slug "lemma", :text "Parallel-loop teams improve through asynchronous work (e.g., researchers + IT)."} {:name "lemma", :name-key "lemma", :slug "lemma", :text "Some connect through tasks (workflow clarity)."} {:name "lemma", :name-key "lemma", :slug "lemma", :text "Some through care (trust, safety)."} {:name "lemma", :name-key "lemma", :slug "lemma", :text "Some through practice (craft, mastery)."} {:name "lemma", :name-key "lemma", :slug "lemma", :text "Some through mission (values, impact)."} {:name "because", :name-key "because", :slug "because", :text "Compatibility Mapping enables collaboration without forcing sameness."} {:name "because", :name-key "because", :slug "because", :text "Different teams require different learning rhythms."} {:name "because", :name-key "because", :slug "because", :text "Each team inhabits a distinct worldshape."} {:name "because", :name-key "because", :slug "because", :text "Boundaries make collaboration healthier, not weaker."} {:name "because", :name-key "because", :slug "because", :text "People connect to work through different modes of intimacy."}], :conclusion "Leadership Patterns Underpinning the Transformation Cycle", :directives {:sigils ["🚴/旦" "🌄/化"], :title "Leadership Patterns Underpinning the Transformation Cycle"}, :id "repository-transition/transformation-engine", :keywords [], :projection-version "flexiarg-v0", :references [], :scores {}, :sigils ["🚴/旦" "🌄/化"], :source-path "library/repository-transition/transformation-engine.flexiarg", :sources [], :status :ok, :title "Leadership Patterns Underpinning the Transformation Cycle", :typed-slots nil} #:pattern{:clauses [{:name "conclusion", :name-key "conclusion", :slug "conclusion", :text "A landscape scan is sharpest when it is (1) anchored to a live mission's named question, (2) split into two instruments — audience-first probing (person/org queries) and concept-research (web) — each used only where its noise profile is low, and (3) read so that even a confirming-negative is a result. The good scan answers a mission's question; it does not forage in general."} {:name "context", :name-key "context", :slug "context", :text "The daily-scan apparatus produces \"something\" every run, which makes \"something\" look like progress even when no real question was asked (the frame-005 discipline-drift diagnosis). A scan day is good not because it found impressive repos but because it moved a specific decision. frame-006 was good on all three axes at once, which is why it is worth encoding."} {:name "IF", :name-key "if", :slug "if", :text "    You are about to run a scan and can either (a) forage the general landscape, or (b) anchor the scan to a live mission's named gap-question with a defined success AND failure criterion — and you have both audience-shaped targets (named people/orgs) and concept-shaped questions (topics/ideas) you'd like to investigate."} {:name "HOWEVER", :name-key "however", :slug "however", :text "    Un-anchored foraging returns output that looks like progress but feeds no decision. And running everything through one instrument fails twice over: a topic-phrased query in a GitHub-probe scan (\"learning-efficiency\") decays to keyword noise, while a named-person query is precisely where the probe shines. Mixing them buries the signal of the good instrument in the noise of the misused one."} {:name "THEN", :name-key "then", :slug "then", :text "    Anchor the scan to one mission's question, stated as a hypothesis whose YES and NO are both informative (\"do the GLAIVE roster's recent repos show learning-efficiency work?\"). Split instruments: run AUDIENCE-FIRST probes (`user:X` / `org:X`) in the scan; route CONCEPT questions (Baldwin effects, learning-efficiency, learnable tactics) to a separate web/research sweep where topic-phrasing belongs. Read a confirming-negative as a finding: \"nobody here owns it\" validated the mission's gap as the operator's own. Then fold the result straight into the mission's MAP."} {:name "BECAUSE", :name-key "because", :slug "because", :text "    Mission-anchoring supplies the named hypothesis the frame-005 discipline demands, externally and for free, and guarantees the result lands somewhere (a mission's MAP) rather than as orphaned \"something.\" The instrument-split keeps each tool in its low-noise regime, so the audience-first signal isn't drowned by topic-noise. And treating the confirming-negative as a result is what lets a scan *validate a gap* — often more valuable than yet another lead, because it tells the operator the territory is theirs."} {:name "NEXT-STEPS", :name-key "next-steps", :slug "next-steps", :text "    - Before probing, write the mission's question as a hypothesis with both outcomes named; if you can't, the scan isn't ready (it would forage).\n    - Sort intended targets into audience-shaped (→ scan probes) and concept-shaped (→ research sweep); never put a topic query in the GitHub scan.\n    - File the frame against the main sequence even when it served one mission (per frame-006: \"not a new series or it gets confusing\"); keep the custom probe set as reusable without registering a standing subseries.\n    - Carry the confirming-negative into the mission's MAP explicitly; a negative that isn't folded back is a wasted scan.\n    - Watch the known blindspot: the `commercial-*` render is a license/homepage heuristic, not a verdict — drill READMEs before judging substance."}], :conclusion "A landscape scan is sharpest when it is (1) anchored to a live mission's named question, (2) split into two instruments — audience-first probing (person/org queries) and concept-research (web) — each used only where its noise profile is low, and (3) read so that even a confirming-negative is a result. The good scan answers a mission's question; it does not forage in general.", :directives {:audience "daily-scan operators (M-daily-scan / run-daily-scan.md), anyone running landscape probes", :keywords ["daily-scan" "mission-anchored" "hypothesis-tested-probe" "audience-first" "concept-research-sweep" "instrument-split" "confirming-negative" "both-outcomes-informative" "frame-006"], :references ["mission-coherence/logic-model-before-code" "eoi-engine/tension-foreclosure"], :sigils ["錨/掃"], :style "pattern", :title "Anchor the Scan to a Live Mission's Question; Split Audience-Probing from Concept-Research", :tone "declarative"}, :id "scan-coherence/mission-anchored-scan", :keywords ["daily-scan" "mission-anchored" "hypothesis-tested-probe" "audience-first" "concept-research-sweep" "instrument-split" "confirming-negative" "both-outcomes-informative" "frame-006"], :projection-version "flexiarg-v0", :references ["mission-coherence/logic-model-before-code" "eoi-engine/tension-foreclosure"], :scores {}, :sigils ["錨/掃"], :source-path "library/scan-coherence/mission-anchored-scan.flexiarg", :sources [], :status :ok, :title "Anchor the Scan to a Live Mission's Question; Split Audience-Probing from Concept-Research", :typed-slots nil} #:pattern{:clauses [{:name "conclusion", :name-key "conclusion", :slug "conclusion", :text "Keep semantic writes append-only with provenance at the store boundary."} {:name "context", :name-key "context", :slug "context", :text "Semantic evolution must be inspectable and reversible."} {:name "IF", :name-key "if", :slug "if", :text "    Proposal or fact updates overwrite prior states."} {:name "HOWEVER", :name-key "however", :slug "however", :text "    You need to revise or retire claims over time."} {:name "THEN", :name-key "then", :slug "then", :text "    Persist every semantic write (proposal, promotion, evidence, action, fact, chain) as append-only\n    records with identifiers and audit metadata, and reject duplicate ids at the store boundary."} {:name "BECAUSE", :name-key "because", :slug "because