ores from XTDB or legacy events, then immediately enforces model invariants on startup and on every write."} {:name "IF", :name-key "if", :slug "if", :text "    `app.store/tx!` runs a verify function on a preview conn and rejects writes when invariants fail, and `app.store-manager` installs the Charon guardian when `MODEL_VERIFY_ON_WRITE` is enabled"} {:name "HOWEVER", :name-key "however", :slug "however", :text "    new or swapped `BASIC_CHAT_DATA_DIR` roots can be missing penholder registry entries, and missing `MODEL_PENHOLDER` values make authorization fail on the very first model descriptor upsert"} {:name "FAILURE-MODES", :name-key "failure-modes", :slug "failure-modes", :text "      penholder missing entry -> invariant failure on first descriptor write\n      unauthorized penholder -> reject writes until registry updated\n      shared data dir across JVMs -> nondeterministic invariants and corruption"} {:name "THEN", :name-key "then", :slug "then", :text "    always enable `MODEL_VERIFY_ON_WRITE` in production, set `MODEL_PENHOLDER`, and run `scripts.charon-penholder-bootstrap` (or equivalent) once per new data root before starting the API; keep `BASIC_CHAT_DATA_DIR` isolated per running JVM"} {:name "IMPLEMENTATION", :name-key "implementation", :slug "implementation", :text "      `apps/graph-memory/src/app/store.clj`: `tx!` forbids `:skip-verify?`, verifies against a preview conn, and throws on invariant failure\n      `apps/graph-memory/src/app/store_manager.clj`: installs `charon-guard/guard-event`, ensures descriptors, and checks invariants at startup\n      `apps/graph-memory/src/app/invariants.clj`: `verify-event` enforces penholder registry membership for model descriptors\n      `apps/graph-memory/src/scripts/charon_penholder_bootstrap.clj`: seeds the penholder registry with model descriptor entries"} {:name "SETTINGS", :name-key "settings", :slug "settings", :text "      BASIC_CHAT_DATA_DIR: data root (unique per JVM)\n      MODEL_PENHOLDER: identity used for penholder certificates (e.g. user)\n      MODEL_VERIFY_ON_WRITE: enable Charon guard on every write (default true)\n      XTDB_CONFIG: path to XTDB config for canonical store"} {:name "BECAUSE", :name-key "because", :slug "because", :text "    the Charon guard provides deterministic rejection of invalid writes, and the penholder registry ensures every model descriptor is authorized and signed before it can mutate the store"} {:name "NEXT-STEPS", :name-key "next-steps", :slug "next-steps", :text "    next[Add a bootstrap hook in dev scripts to seed penholder registry on empty data dirs.]\n    next[Surface penholder/invariant failures as explicit stack blockers in triage logs.]"}], :conclusion "  keep Futon1 storage coherent by enforcing Charon-guarded invariant checks on every write, requiring a penholder registry entry for each model descriptor, and bootstrapping the penholder registry before first write to a new data dir", :directives {:audience "futon stewards, stack maintainers", :factor "Keen investigation (dhammavicaya)", :references ["stack-coherence/futon1-determinism" "sidecar/validation-enforcement-gate" "repository-transition/invariants"], :sigils ["🗿/正"], :title "Futon1 Storage Coherence Guard", :tone "analytic-neutral"}, :id "stack-coherence/futon1-storage-coherence", :keywords [], :projection-version "flexiarg-v0", :references ["stack-coherence/futon1-determinism" "sidecar/validation-enforcement-gate" "repository-transition/invariants"], :scores {}, :sigils ["🗿/正"], :source-path "library/stack-coherence/futon1-storage-coherence.flexiarg", :sources [], :status :ok, :title "Futon1 Storage Coherence Guard", :typed-slots nil} #:pattern{:clauses [{:name "conclusion", :name-key "conclusion", :slug "conclusion", :text "  for each prototype with a :maturity tag, verify that evidence supports the claimed level; flag mismatches and emit promotion or demotion recommendations"} {:name "context", :name-key "context", :slug "context", :text "Prototypes claim maturity levels (:stub, :greenfield, :active, :settled) but these claims can drift from reality."} {:name "IF", :name-key "if", :slug "if", :text "    devmap prototypes carry :maturity tags indicating their readiness level"} {:name "HOWEVER", :name-key "however", :slug "however", :text "    maturity claims are often aspirational — a prototype tagged :active may have failing tests, and one tagged :stub may actually be running in production"} {:name "THEN", :name-key "then", :slug "then", :text "    for each prototype with a :maturity tag, verify that evidence supports the claimed level; flag mismatches and emit promotion or demotion recommendations"} {:name "AUDIT-CRITERIA", :name-key "audit-criteria", :slug "audit-criteria", :text "      :stub claims valid if: no runnable implementation exists\n      :greenfield claims valid if: code exists but no end-to-end test evidence\n      :active claims valid if: runs end-to-end, has 3+ logged uses, PSR/PUR evidence\n      :settled claims valid if: 10+ uses, >80% success rate, no regressions in 2 weeks"} {:name "MISMATCH-ACTIONS", :name-key "mismatch-actions", :slug "mismatch-actions", :text "      over-claimed (e.g., :active but no evidence) → demote and flag for attention\n      under-claimed (e.g., :stub but has passing tests) → recommend promotion\n      no-tag (missing :maturity) → flag for classification"} {:name "BECAUSE", :name-key "because", :slug "because", :text "    maturity tags are trust signals — downstream consumers decide what to depend on based on claimed maturity, so false claims cause silent breakage"} {:name "NEXT-STEPS", :name-key "next-steps", :slug "next-steps", :text "    next[Run maturity audit on all devmap prototypes; generate mismatch report.]\n    next[Add :maturity tags to any prototype missing them.]\n    next[Wire maturity changes into sidecar logs for audit trail.]\n    next[Review maturity mismatches in weekly stack triage.]"}], :conclusion "  for each prototype with a :maturity tag, veri