d backfill pathways", :directives {:audience "storage maintainers, futon1a builders", :factor "Keen investigation (dhammavicaya)", :keywords ["invariants" "repair" "backfill" "cleanup"], :references ["stack-coherence/evidence-ledger" "storage/rapid-debugging"], :sigils ["🎶/口"], :title "Invariants vs Repair", :tone "formal-analytic"}, :id "storage/invariants-vs-repair", :keywords ["invariants" "repair" "backfill" "cleanup"], :projection-version "flexiarg-v0", :references ["stack-coherence/evidence-ledger" "storage/rapid-debugging"], :scores {}, :sigils ["🎶/口"], :source-path "library/storage/invariants-vs-repair.flexiarg", :sources [], :status :ok, :title "Invariants vs Repair", :typed-slots nil} #:pattern{:clauses [{:name "conclusion", :name-key "conclusion", :slug "conclusion", :text "  allow background knowledge ingest to accumulate in the same persistent store outside interactive sessions"} {:name "context", :name-key "context", :slug "context", :text "futon1’s devmap positions open-world ingest as a core way to build shared knowledge."} {:name "IF", :name-key "if", :slug "if", :text "    knowledge needs to accumulate beyond interactive sessions"} {:name "HOWEVER", :name-key "however", :slug "however", :text "    separate stores or session-only ingestion fragment the graph"} {:name "THEN", :name-key "then", :slug "then", :text "    ingest open-world data into the same persistent store with the same invariants"} {:name "BECAUSE", :name-key "because", :slug "because", :text "    background knowledge must remain queryable and coherent with session data"} {:name "NEXT-STEPS", :name-key "next-steps", :slug "next-steps", :text "    next[Define open-world ingest contracts and validation rules for futon1a.]\n    next[Add tests verifying open-world data survives restart and is queryable.]"}], :conclusion "  allow background knowledge ingest to accumulate in the same persistent store outside interactive sessions", :directives {:audience "futon1a builders, ingest maintainers", :factor "Keen investigation (dhammavicaya)", :keywords ["open-world" "background ingest" "continuity" "persistent store"], :references ["stack-coherence/evidence-ledger"], :sigils ["📥/入"], :title "Open-World Continuity", :tone "formal-analytic"}, :id "storage/open-world-continuity", :keywords ["open-world" "background ingest" "continuity" "persistent store"], :projection-version "flexiarg-v0", :references ["stack-coherence/evidence-ledger"], :scores {}, :sigils ["📥/入"], :source-path "library/storage/open-world-continuity.flexiarg", :sources [], :status :ok, :title "Open-World Continuity", :typed-slots nil} #:pattern{:clauses [{:name "conclusion", :name-key "conclusion", :slug "conclusion", :text "  if you want rapid open-world ingest but also coherent state, validate aggressively and provide repair tooling"} {:name "context", :name-key "context", :slug "context", :text "futon1 hardened open-world ingest and added repair scripts after ingest drift."} {:name "IF", :name-key "if", :slug "if", :text "    you want to ingest background knowledge quickly"} {:name "HOWEVER", :name-key "however", :slug "however", :text "    you also need open-world data to remain coherent and mirrorable"} {:name "THEN", :name-key "then", :slug "then", :text "    enforce strict validation on ingest and supply repair/backfill scripts for recovery"} {:name "BECAUSE", :name-key "because", :slug "because", :text "    unvalidated open-world ingest caused drift and required repair pathways"} {:name "NEXT-STEPS", :name-key "next-steps", :slug "next-steps", :text "    next[Define open-world validation rules and error reporting.]\n    next[Add tests that assert open-world fields are mirrored into XTDB.]"}], :conclusion "  if you want rapid open-world ingest but also coherent state, validate aggressively and provide repair tooling", :directives {:audience "storage maintainers, futon1a builders", :factor "Keen investigation (dhammavicaya)", :keywords ["open-world" "ingest" "validation" "repair"], :references ["stack-coherence/evidence-ledger" "storage/open-world-continuity"], :sigils ["📥/入"], :title "Open-World Velocity vs Validation", :tone "formal-analytic"}, :id "storage/open-world-velocity-validation", :keywords ["open-world" "ingest" "validation" "repair"], :projection-version "flexiarg-v0", :references ["stack-coherence/evidence-ledger" "storage/open-world-continuity"], :scores {}, :sigils ["📥/入"], :source-path "library/storage/open-world-velocity-validation.flexiarg", :sources [], :status :ok, :title "Open-World Velocity vs Validation", :typed-slots nil} #:pattern{:clauses [{:name "conclusion", :name-key "conclusion", :slug "conclusion", :text "  if you want durability but also fast access, mirror XTDB into Datascript and enforce reproducible alignment as a hard contract"} {:name "context", :name-key "context", :slug "context", :text "futon1 repeatedly fixed XTDB mirroring to prevent drift and metadata loss."} {:name "IF", :name-key "if", :slug "if", :text "    you want the database to be persistent"} {:name "HOWEVER", :name-key "however", :slug "however", :text "    you also want access to be fast"} {:name "THEN", :name-key "then", :slug "then", :text "    mirror XTDB into Datascript with explicit mirroring rules and tests"} {:name "BECAUSE", :name-key "because", :slug "because", :text "    mirroring without enforcement creates drift across restarts and environments"} {:name "NEXT-STEPS", :name-key "next-steps", :slug "next-steps", :text "    next[Define the mirror invariants and verify them on every restart cycle.]\n    next[Add tests that assert metadata parity between XTDB and Datascript.]"}], :conclusion "  if you want durability but also fast access, mirror XTDB into Datascript and enforce reproducible alignment as a hard contract", :directives {:audience "storage maintainers, futon1a builders", :factor "Keen investigation (dhammavicaya)", :keywords ["persistence" "speed" "datascript" "xtdb" "mirroring"], :references ["stack-coherence/evidence-ledger" "storage/reproducible-mirroring"], :sigils ["🍵/文"], :title "Persistence-Speed Mirroring", :tone "formal-analytic"}, :id "storage/persistence-speed-mirroring", :keywords ["persistence" "speed" "datascript" "xtdb" "mirroring"], :projection-version "flexiarg-v0", :references ["stack-coherence/evidence-ledger" "storage/reproducible-mirroring"], :scores {}, :sigils ["🍵/文"], :source-path "library/storage/persistence-speed-mirroring.flexiarg", :sources [], :status :ok, :title "Persistence-Speed Mirroring", :typed-slots nil} #:pattern{:clauses [{:name "conclusion", :name-key "conclusion", :slug "conclusion", :text "  acknowledge writes only after the canonical store is durably committed and the written documents are queryable (read-your-write)"} {:name "context", :name-key "context", :slug "context", :text "interactive QA found items (lyrics) present in futon1’s durable event log while missing from the queryable XTDB materialization; the user experience was “it was saved” but reads returned nothing."} {:name "IF", :name-key "if", :slug "if", :text "    a write can be accepted/recorded without guaranteeing it becomes queryable in the canonical store"} {:name "HOWEVER", :name-key "however", :slug "however", :text "    event-log truth can diverge from canonical truth and the system will behave as if data is missing (often discovered only in interactive QA)"} {:name "THEN", :name-key "then", :slug "then", :text "    gate success responses on both:\n    1) durable commit confirmation\n    2) postcommit materialization verification (the put docs can be read back by id)"} {:name "BECAUSE", :name-key "because", :slug "because", :text "    without a postcommit read-your-write gate, “accepted but not ingested/materialized” becomes a silent failure mode that accumulates repair debt and erodes trust in the storage contract"} {:name "NEXT-STEPS", :name-key "next-steps", :slug "next-steps", :text "    next[Add an end-to-end QA checklist item: write -> immediate read-by-id -> restart -> read-by-id.]\n    next[If an event log exists, specify it as audit-only unless a catch-up invariant proves “caught up” with canonical state.]"}], :conclusion "  acknowledge writes only after the canonical store is durably committed and the written documents are queryable (read-your-write)", :directives {:audience "storage maintainers, futon1a builders", :factor "Keen investigation (dhammavicaya)", :keywords ["durability" "materialization" "read-your-write" "event-log" "ack" "storage"], :references ["stack-coherence/evidence-ledger" "storage/durability-first" "storage/canonical-interface"], :sigils ["💎/石"], :title "Postcommit Materialization Gate", :tone "analytic-neutral"}, :id "storage/postcommit-materialization-gate", :keywords ["durability" "materialization" "read-your-write" "event-log" "ack" "storage"], :projection-version "flexiarg-v0", :references ["stack-coherence/evidence-ledger" "storage/durability-first" "storage/canonical-interface"], :scores {}, :sigils ["💎/石"], :source-path "library/storage/postcommit-materialization-gate.flexiarg", :sources [], :status :ok, :title "Postcommit Materialization Gate", :typed-slots nil} #:pattern{:clauses [{:name "conclusion", :name-key "conclusion", :slug "conclusion", :text "  make storage failures diagnosable in minutes through explicit diagnostics and proof tests"} {:name "context", :name-key "context", :slug "context", :text "futon1 repeatedly needed diagnostics and tests to keep storage behavior legible."} {:name "IF", :name-key "if", :slug "if", :text "    failures lack traceable context (layer, operation, entity, expected vs actual)"} {:name "HOWEVER", :name-key "however", :slug "however", :text "    debugging requires ad hoc spelunking and slow recovery cycles"} {:name "THEN", :name-key "then", :slug "then", :text "    attach explicit diagnostics to all storage errors and prove invariants with targeted tests"} {:name "BECAUSE", :name-key "because", :slug "because", :text "    futon1 fixes show that diagnostics