nected story-world do for X?”) and each yielding stories, participant feedback, and a short interpretive report."} {:name "BECAUSE", :name-key "because", :slug "because", :text "    Proof through pilots turns the business plan into a sequence of situated experiments whose successes—and failures—offer persuasive material for future commissions and follow-on funding."} {:name "NEXT-STEPS", :name-key "next-steps", :slug "next-steps", :text "    next[Define the first pilot question and the evidence you will capture.]\n    next[Draft a template for the interpretive report delivered after each pilot.]\n    next[Define what counts as proof (e.g., measurable changes in shared insight or coordination) and a falsifier.]"}], :conclusion "  Structure development around a small constellation of pilots, each framed as a question (“What can a connected story-world do for X?”) and each yielding stories, participant feedback, and a short interpretive report.", :directives {:audience "funders, project stewards, evaluators", :sigils ["🌆/亏" "💬/上"], :style "design-pattern", :title "Proof Through Pilots", :tone "analytic"}, :id "vsatlas/proof-through-pilots", :keywords [], :projection-version "flexiarg-v0", :references [], :scores {}, :sigils ["🌆/亏" "💬/上"], :source-path "library/vsatlas/proof-through-pilots.flexiarg", :sources [], :status :ok, :title "Proof Through Pilots", :typed-slots nil} #:pattern{:clauses [{:name "conclusion", :name-key "conclusion", :slug "conclusion", :text "  Use cross-story arcs to convert individual testimony into distributed reasons and, ultimately, coordinated causes."} {:name "context", :name-key "context", :slug "context", :text "Relational links between stories can transform individual testimony into shared motivation and coordinated collective action. This does not apply when groups explicitly reject collective action."} {:name "IF", :name-key "if", :slug "if", :text "    Individual stories provide reasons but remain isolated and unrecognised by peers."} {:name "HOWEVER", :name-key "however", :slug "however", :text "    Social agency requires resonance, alignment, and shared sensemaking."} {:name "THEN", :name-key "then", :slug "then", :text "    Use cross-story arcs to convert individual testimony into distributed reasons and, ultimately, coordinated causes."} {:name "BECAUSE", :name-key "because", :slug "because", :text "    Relational topology is the missing gear train that turns narrative into collective action."} {:name "NEXT-STEPS", :name-key "next-steps", :slug "next-steps", :text "    next[Map two existing story clusters and identify the first arc that could connect them.]\n    next[Draft a facilitation prompt that surfaces shared motifs across the clusters.]\n    next[Define a success signal (e.g., a coordinated action emerged) and a failure signal (e.g., links created but no shared action).]"}], :conclusion "  Use cross-story arcs to convert individual testimony into distributed reasons and, ultimately, coordinated causes.", :directives {:audience "cognitive designers, social-systems architects", :sigils ["⚡️/力" "📥/几"], :style "design-pattern", :title "Reasons-to-Causes Gear Train", :tone "analytic"}, :id "vsatlas/reasons-to-causes", :keywords [], :projection-version "flexiarg-v0", :references [], :scores {}, :sigils ["⚡️/力" "📥/几"], :source-path "library/vsatlas/reasons-to-causes.flexiarg", :sources [], :status :ok, :title "Reasons-to-Causes Gear Train", :typed-slots nil} #:pattern{:clauses [{:name "conclusion", :name-key "conclusion", :slug "conclusion", :text "  Articulate a shared stewardship compact that clarifies which parts of VSATLAS are commons (open protocols, core code), which are services (facilitation, training, customisation), and how partners can participate in governance over time."} {:name "context", :name-key "context", :slug "context", :text "You are defining how ownership, responsibility, and governance are shared so partners can commit to a shared effort, without relying on a single founder or lab. This does not apply to short-lived experiments with no governance commitments."} {:name "IF", :name-key "if", :slug "if", :text "    Early-stage platforms often rely on one or two overburdened founders who are expected to be visionaries, engineers, salespeople, and custodians."} {:name "HOWEVER", :name-key "however", :slug "however", :text "    Concentrating all ownership and responsibility undermines resilience and makes partners wary of long-term dependence on a single individual or lab."} {:name "THEN", :name-key "then", :slug "then", :text "    Articulate a shared stewardship compact that clarifies which parts of VSATLAS are commons (open protocols, core code), which are services (facilitation, training, customisation), and how partners can participate in governance over time."} {:name "BECAUSE", :name-key "because", :slug "because", :text "    A clear compact reassures institutions, invites co-ownership, and aligns the business model with the manifold’s deeper claim: that worlds worth living in are co-created and co-stewarded."} {:name "NEXT-STEPS", :name-key "next-steps", :slug "next-steps", :text "    next[Draft the compact as a one-page charter and circulate to anchor partners.]\n    next[Define a first governance checkpoint and the decision rights it covers.]\n    next[Define evidence signals (e.g., signed charter, shared decision logs) and a failure case (e.g., partners decline co-ownership).]"}], :conclusion "  Articulate a shared stewardship compact that clarifies which parts of VSATLAS are commons (open protocols, core code), which are services (facilitation, training, customisation), and how partners can participate in governance over time.", :directives {:audience "collaborators, anchor institutions, advanced contributors", :sigils ["🚴/公" "🌈/也"], :style "design-pattern", :title "Shared Stewardship Compact", :tone "analytic"}, :id "vsatlas/shared-stewardship-compact", :keywords [], :projection-version "flexiarg-v0", :references [], :scores {}, :sigils ["🚴/公" "🌈/也"], :source-path "library/vsatlas/shared-stewardship-compact.flexiarg", :sources [], :status :ok, :title "Shared Stewardship Compact", :typed-slots nil} #:pattern{:clauses [{:name "conclusion", :name-key "conclusion", :slug "conclusion", :text "  Introduce a stewardship layer—human or automated roles that approve, edit, or retire arcs based on clear criteria."} {:name "context", :name-key "context", :slug "context", :text "You need explicit roles or processes to curate and manage links, so openness does not undermine coherence or safety. This does not apply when contribution volume is low and trust is already high."} {:name "IF", :name-key "if", :slug "if", :text "    Open contribution environments generate noise, drift, and potential misuse."} {:name "HOWEVER", :name-key "however", :slug "however", :text "    Accepting every proposed link collapses the manifold into clutter or abuse."} {:name "THEN", :name-key "then", :slug "then", :text "    Introduce a stewardship layer—human or automated roles that approve, edit, or retire arcs based on clear criteria."} {:name "BECAUSE", :name-key "because", :slug "because", :text "    Stewardship preserves coherence, safety, and long-term navigability."} {:name "NEXT-STEPS", :name-key "next-steps", :slug "next-steps", :text "    next[Define a minimal stewardship checklist for approving new arcs.]\n    next[Name the first steward role and the threshold for retirement.]\n    next[Define a volume signal (e.g., links/day) that triggers stewardship activation.]"}], :conclusion "  Introduce a stewardship layer—human or automated roles that approve, edit, or retire arcs based on clear criteria.", :directives {:audience "governance designers, multi-agent architects", :sigils ["👥/义" "💢/力"], :style "design-pattern", :title "Stewardship Layer", :tone "analytic"}, :id "vsatlas/stewardship-layer", :keywords [], :projection-version "flexiarg-v0", :references [], :scores {}, :sigils ["👥/义" "💢/力"], :source-path "library/vsatlas/stewardship-layer.flexiarg", :sources [], :status :ok, :title "Stewardship Layer", :typed-slots nil} #:pattern{:clauses [{:name "conclusion", :name-key "conclusion", :slug "conclusion", :text "  Model the manifold as an emporium—an interior space where sovereign stories gain new meaning through adjacency and optional relations."} {:name "context", :name-key "context", :slug "context", :text "You are framing the 'story manifold' as a shared interior where stories remain sovereign, but gain meaning through proximity and (optional) relationships. This does not apply when stories must be tightly merged into a single authored narrative."} {:name "IF", :name-key "if", :slug "if", :text "    Stories remain fixed artifacts with no shared environment."} {:name "HOWEVER", :name-key "however", :slug "however", :text "    Vibrant ecosystems emerge when independent narrative units coexist in proximity."} {:name "THEN", :name-key "then", :slug "then", :text "    Model the manifold as an emporium—an interior space where sovereign stories gain new meaning through adjacency and optional relations."} {:name "BECAUSE", :name-key "because", :slug "because", :text "    Proximity, not centralisation, generates aliveness, cross-pollination, and emergent understanding."} {:name "NEXT-STEPS", :name-key "next-steps", :slug "next-steps", :text "    next[Sketch one emporium map that shows how three stories could sit adjacent without merging.]\n    next[Define a minimal “adjacency” link type that preserves sovereignty.]\n    next[Define an evidence signal (e.g., new cross-story references after adjacency) and a falsifier (e.g., no uptake of adjacency links).]\n    next[Consolidate with vsatlas/non-destructive-relational-layers and retire this pattern once merged.]"}], :conclusion "  Model the manifold as an emporium—an interior space where sovereign stories gain new meaning through adjacency and optional relations.", :directives {:audience "experience designers, relational infrastruct